This product includes software developed for the Abrams Event Address (AEA) project.

Cryptographic component:
- src/sha256.rs is a self-contained, zero-allocation implementation of SHA-256 as
  specified in NIST FIPS 180-4, written for this project. It does not depend on the
  external `sha2` crate or any third-party cryptography library.
- It is tested against the NIST FIPS 180-4 example vectors ("", "abc", and the
  two-block 448-bit message) in src/sha256.rs, and against Python hashlib through
  tests/kat/vectors.txt.
- It is NOT a CAVP/ACVP-validated or CMVP (FIPS 140) certified module.

